{"duration_api_ms":275374,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5c26ed43-c1e1-4bc7-b00d-7a8847d1c9c8","total_cost_usd":1.7749293999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":74,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78395,"cache_read_input_tokens":3131467,"output_tokens":26059,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4070},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78395,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1239,"cache_read_input_tokens":110378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":355},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":74,"outputTokens":26059,"cacheReadInputTokens":3131467,"cacheCreationInputTokens":78395,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.7749293999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4070,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":78395,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":37,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I measured repaint per keystroke and per remote change on large-100p.docx, recorded the results in `baseline.md`, and committed the work as `ac3ddef`. All six acceptance commands pass, and so do `theseus validate` (0 errors, 4 warnings) and `theseus scope-check`.\n\n**What I did:** I wrote `.theseus/oracle/perf/word-repaint.js`. It builds the fork with `differential/build.sh`, injects the bundle by Playwright routing the way PKT-0093 did, and opens the file as users A and B. On the live editor it wraps the recalculation, redraw and paint entry points and the canvas `drawImage` calls, and records who called each one. I ran 2 runs of 20 events per side (local typing measured on A, remote changes measured on B), with one page visible.\n\n**Findings:**\n- **Redraw always works on whole pages.** Nothing is invalidated in smaller rectangles. A dirty page is fully redrawn into its cached image, glyph by glyph (about 2,000 offscreen `drawImage` calls per page), then copied to the screen once (`OnPaint`, about 1.8 copies per event).\n- **Who decides the range:**\n  - Typing goes through the fast recalculation paths (`private_RecalculateFastParagraph` / `FastRunRange`) and recalculates 1–2 pages.\n  - `OnRecalculatePage` itself marks only the changed page dirty. `CDocument.Redraw` and `OnRepaintPage` are never called during typing.\n  - `CWordCollaborativeEditing.Send_Changes` calls `ClearCachePages(); FirePaint()` on every send while more than one user is editing (\"to redraw locks\"). That invalidates every page and redraws the visible page a second time.\n- **Ceiling for the lock-redraw clear:** I measured it by turning that call off at runtime (`NOCLEAR=1`). This is an upper bound, not a fix. For local typing, pages redrawn per keystroke drop from 1.8 to 1 and paint time from 30 to 18 ms (about 40%). Remote changes show no gain: B still redraws twice because of its own recalculations.\n- **Remote full-document recalculation:** 4–5 of the 40 remote events leave the fast path and recalculate all 86 pages, at 260–420 ms each. That accounts for the whole remote recalculation average.\n- **Redrawing only the changed lines:** I estimate it would save about 9 ms per local keystroke and about 15 ms per remote event. This is an estimate; I did not prototype it.\n\n**Not measured:**\n- The remote fast-path recalculation isn't timed (I didn't wrap that function). So the remote recalc median of 0 ms means \"not measured\", not \"no work\"; `baseline.md` says so.\n- I didn't commit the per-event JSON results because of the 6-file budget. The script's `--json` option reproduces them.\n- I made no changes in `external/sdkjs`.\n\n**Follow-ups requested** (in `.theseus/spawn/`):\n1. A refactor: skip the all-pages lock redraw in `Send_Changes` when no lock changed.\n2. An investigation: find out why some remote changes fall back to recalculating the whole document.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** the word editor redraws by whole page. A dirty page's cached image is fully redrawn and then copied to the screen. Typing marks pages dirty through `OnRecalculatePage`, and co-editing adds an all-pages clear in `Send_Changes` on every send. The PKT-0093 routing harness had never been committed, so I rebuilt it from the descriptions in `baseline.md`; it is now part of `word-repaint.js`.","ttft_ms":3333,"type":"result","duration_ms":907329,"uuid":"fc6a7b77-5084-44b2-a772-28fe59cc3e46","ttft_stream_ms":2189,"time_to_request_ms":310,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":201,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":5,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":105,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":107,"time_to_request_major_faults":16,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":209,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":137,"process_rss_mib_result":250,"process_anon_mib_result":161,"process_peak_rss_mib":286,"process_cpu_ms_